Recovered identity:
Visualize is the spatial knowledge workbench inside Knowledge & Learning. It visualizes canonical objects and relationships; it does not own a second canonical object graph merely because it renders one.
View identity:
- Tree = constrained canonical hierarchy/navigation representation.
- Path = ordered/path/progression grammar.
- Graph = semantic relationship exploration.
- Canvas = free spatial representation/presentation workspace.
Architecture:
VisualizeWorkspaceCore / SpatialInteractionCore
→ TreeViewAdapter
→ PathViewAdapter
→ GraphViewAdapter
→ CanvasViewAdapter
Shared spatial mechanics recovered:
- selection + primary focus + selected set;
- multi-selection where admitted;
- pointer hit testing;
- keyboard object/edge navigation;
- viewport/camera state;
- pan / zoom / fit;
- context actions;
- inspector synchronization;
- overlays/transient spatial tools;
- presentation-state Undo/Redo;
- accessible interaction;
- RTL/Bidi-safe chrome while world geometry remains coordinate-direction neutral.
Canonical vs representation law:
Canvas representation state must be separate from canonical object/relation state. A production-mappable representation identity is:
representationId → canonicalObjectId + coordinates + presentation state
Consequences:
- same canonical object may have multiple Canvas representations;
- duplicate representation != duplicate canonical object;
- remove from Canvas != delete canonical object;
- Canvas-only links != canonical relationship mutation;
- moving representations does not mutate containment;
- canonical mutation remains authority-gated unless separately opened.
